Z||000000||RossT||01-16-2001||01:07 AM||||anyone know of an online source for kenwood<BR>speakers other than Crutchfield.<P>looking for 4x10 kfc-415c<BR>            4x6  kfc-x466c<P>Crutchfield wants $99 for each of the above.<P>Thanks, Ross||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-16-2001||01:40 AM||||This is where I bought many Items on-line. A lot cheaper than Crutchfield.<BR>The KFC-415C's are only $74.00<BR>KFC-X466C's  Are $69.00. <BR>The 4X6's are under the Kenwood Excelon tab and the 4X10's are under the Kenwood tab. (on right side of their page)<P><BR><A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||01-16-2001||02:02 AM||||Thank Oreif, That was fast! I will check into it. One last question, whats the best way to wire into the factory speaker harness without have to splice (cut) wires.  I want to be able to slip the stock speakers back in if I ever want to sell.  I know Crutfield sends along a harness for the speakers they sell.<P>Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-16-2001||02:15 AM||||I only have seen the speaker adapters at Crutchfield. I haven't seen them anywhere else. I think they charge $2.00 each if you don't order speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||01-26-2001||02:39 AM||||Well the kenwoods came in the mail today.  Very Very nice and much cheaper that Crutchfield.<P>Thanks Oreif!  <P>Now lets see if I have this correct.  The factory gm speaker wires: The darker wires are + , and the lighter wires are - .||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-26-2001||02:45 AM||||Yes, Dark is +<BR>Light is -||||reg||14
Z||000006||RossT||02-06-2001||12:43 AM||||Just got the Kenwoods in today.  OH MY G...<BR>do they sound good. That has to be the easiest and cheapest improvement in sound that I have ever heard. I did get the gm  speaker wire harness adapeters from crutchfield, but they made the job so simple.  Only real problem was the capaciter on the kenwoods 4X6 had to be moved in order to fit them into the 4X6 fiero frame.<P>Next job will be to install the Grand Prix CD player....||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||02-06-2001||01:14 AM||||Just go to <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.newellelectronics.com</A>  and they can supply you with an adapter harness to hook the GP stereo into the Fiero harness. No cutting/splicing required!<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||William||02-06-2001||08:12 AM||||Oreif,<BR>I've just discovered that the wires going to the seat speakers are different. It appears that the lighter wires are +. At least I hope so or I've really screwed up....||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||02-06-2001||10:03 AM||||William, Are you sure? I don't have an 84/85 book that covers those wires. I have a Haynes which shows the dark as + and the light as - coming out of the radio and GM is pretty anal about keeping wires dark/light. Does anyone have an 84/85 service manual to see how the seats are wired? I have always wired them + is dark and haven't had a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000010||William||02-06-2001||11:52 AM||||Here's what I found. The speakers have a A and B terminal. On the front speakers, the darker wires go to terminal A. On the seat speakers, The darker wires were connected to terminal B. Who's got a diagram?||||reg||1
Z||000011||RossT||02-06-2001||11:51 PM||||When I got the crutchfield speaker adapters (84-88 fiero all years) they would only snap into the factory speaker harnes as + to dark wire and - to light wire. I did notice however that when I took the 4X6's out they were labled with a +/- termanal and the one foot wire leads from the factory speaker were black to - and orange to +, but they did plug into the factory harness as OREIF has stated.  ||||reg||1
